WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.805
The drift engine compares the
estate with a versioned record,

2
00:00:03.805 --> 00:00:08.150
so an approved change isn't drift and
any finding can be re-derived later.

3
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:13.238
Severity is computed from the kind of drift
and whether the thing is in active use.

4
00:00:13.238 --> 00:00:16.410
A critical finding halts
and alerts a named person,

5
00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.600
and it's never fixed automatically.

6
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.782
The engine never edits the record,

7
00:00:20.782 --> 00:00:24.600
never judges whether a rule is
right, and never accepts risk.

8
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.413
And be precise with assessors:
some checks are automated today,

9
00:00:28.413 --> 00:00:30.613
and others are still found by people.

10
00:00:30.613 --> 00:00:35.215
The riskiest change is to what counts as
drift, so the decision: any change to

11
00:00:35.215 --> 00:00:40.263
the classifier or its thresholds gets a
reviewer from outside the program office.

12
00:00:40.263 --> 00:00:41.950
Next, who governs.
